## Security Hardening Measures

### 1. Cloudflare WAF Custom Block Rules

Lament deploys custom Cloudflare Web Application Firewall (WAF) expression rules to immediately drop requests targeting sensitive paths, environment configurations, SSH keys, database dumps, admin probes, and unauthorized `/hls/` hotlinking.

```sql
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.env") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.git/config") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.git/HEAD") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/wp-config.php") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.htaccess") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.htpasswd") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.ssh/id_rsa") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.aws/credentials") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/docker-compose.yml") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/web.config") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/id_rsa") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/credentials.json") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/secrets.yml") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/secrets.yaml") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.npmrc") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.gitlab-ci.yml") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/cmd_") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/cmd.") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/shell") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/phpmyadmin") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/xmlrpc.php") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/wp-admin") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/wp-login") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/eval-stdin") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/vendor/") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/composer.") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/backup") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/install.php") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/setup.php") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/admin.php") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/configuration.php") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.svn/") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.DS_Store") or
(http.request.uri.path contains ".sql") or
(http.request.uri.path contains ".bak") or
(http.request.uri.path contains ".old") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/phpunit/") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.vscode/") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.idea/") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "database.sqlite") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.env.local") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.env.production") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.env.backup") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.git/") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.hg/") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.aws/config") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.azure/") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.docker/config.json") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.kube/config") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "serviceaccount.json") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.netrc") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.travis.yml") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.circleci/") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/.yarnrc") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "Pipfile") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "dump.sql") or
(http.request.uri.path contains ".sql.gz") or
(http.request.uri.path contains ".mdb") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "jwt.json") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "auth.json") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/actuator") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/server-status") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/server-info") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/_profiler") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/telescope") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/console") or
(http.request.uri.path contains "/hls/" and not (http.referer contains "lament.rynds.my.id" or http.referer contains "localhost" or http.referer contains "127.0.0.1" or http.referer == ""))
```

Key features of this WAF block rule:

- **Direct `/hls/` Hotlinking Protection**: Blocks direct requests to `/hls/` unless the request header `http.referer` contains the authorized domain (`lament.rynds.my.id`), local dev server (`localhost`), or native mobile apps (empty referer).
- **Environment & Secret Defense**: Immediately drops requests probing for `.env`, `wp-config.php`, `id_rsa`, `credentials.json`, `secrets.yml`, `.aws/credentials`, `database.sqlite`, `dump.sql`, or `.bak` files.
- **Admin & Vulnerability Probe Filtering**: Drops bot traffic scanning for `/wp-admin`, `/phpmyadmin`, `/actuator`, `/_profiler`, `/telescope`, or `/console`.

---

## 2. Cloudflare Global Rate Limiting WAF Rule

To protect all subdomains (`rynds.my.id`) under Cloudflare's single Rate Limiting rule constraint, Lament uses a targeted Rate Limiting rule:

```sql
http.host eq "api.lament.rynds.my.id"
```

### Rate Limiting Parameters:
- **Rate Threshold**: `15 requests` per `10 seconds` per IP (or `60 requests` per `1 minute`)
- **Action**: `Block (429)` or `Managed Challenge`

> [!TIP]
> Setting the Rate Limiter at the Cloudflare Edge network drops excessive bot spam and load-test flooding before requests reach Cloudflare Workers, keeping daily Worker request usage at 0.

---

## 3. Anti-Scraping Direct Access Guard

Frontend SvelteKit proxies inspect browser `Sec-Fetch-Dest` and `Sec-Fetch-Mode` HTTP headers on all `/api/` endpoints:

- **Direct Browser Navigation Block**: Requests with `sec-fetch-dest: document` or `sec-fetch-mode: navigate` (triggered when a user types `/api/tracks` directly into a browser URL address bar) are immediately blocked with HTTP 403 Forbidden.
- **Internal Fetch Passthrough**: Application `fetch()` calls (`sec-fetch-dest: empty` and `sec-fetch-mode: cors`) pass through seamlessly for authorized web app users.

---

## 4. Query & Limit Sanitization

Pagination parameters (`?limit=`) are strictly capped (max 30 on frontend proxies, max 50 on backend API) to prevent bulk JSON data harvesting dumps.

---

## 5. Constant-Time Key Comparison

To prevent timing side-channel attacks when verifying `X-Master-Key`, `auth.middleware.ts` uses Web Crypto HMAC constant-time binary comparison (`crypto.subtle.sign`).

---

## 6. CORS Policy & Local Development

Allowed origins are dynamically validated at request time based on the `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` environment variable in production.

- **Production Origins**: Only origins listed in `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (`lament.rynds.my.id`, `docs.lament.rynds.my.id`, `dash.lament.rynds.my.id`) receive `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` headers.
- **Local Development**: Origins matching `http://localhost:*` or `http://127.0.0.1:*` are automatically allowed in development to enable dev server communication.
